\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One even rotational link on 4 sites}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Take #{X=(\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z)^2} and the internal plane
of \ref{fdip-00YF}. Assign the even element #{R=e_1e_2} of
\ref{fdip-00YJ} to the labeled edge #{((0,0),1)}, and assign
#{1} to every other positive labeled edge. All translation
components may be zero. The internal exterior factor has rank
#{4}; the total cubical exterior factor also has rank #{4}.
The 4 sites therefore give a fixed free cochain module of rank
##{4\cdot4\cdot4=64.}
Its counting pairing is perfect over #{\mathbb Z} and positive
definite over #{\mathbb Q}.}

\p{For a cubical degree-zero field supported at #{(1,0)} with
internal value #{e_1}, the transported value at #{(0,0)} is
#{(T_1^Rf)(0,0)=A(R)^{-1}e_1=-e_1}. Replacing that link by
#{1} would give #{e_1}. Internal degree changes neither the
site label nor the cubical cell direction.}
